  "result": "Excellent! All 106 tests pass. I've successfully added VAT calculations to the invoicing system:\n\n**Updated src/invoices.js:**\n- `invoiceTotals()` now returns `{ subtotal, discount, vat, total }`\n- VAT is calculated per line: `(lineAmount - lineDiscount) \u00d7 vatRate / 100`, rounded with `roundCents()`\n- Total invoice VAT = sum of all line VATs (not a percentage of total)\n- Formula: `total = subtotal - discount + vat`\n- All amounts clamped at 0\n\n**Updated src/render.js:**\n- Shows breakdown lines when there's any discount or VAT:\n  - Subtotal\n  - Discount (if > 0)\n  - VAT (if > 0)\n  - Total\n- All amounts formatted with `formatEuros()`\n\n**Key behavior:**\n- VAT calculated per line on the discounted amount\n- Different VAT rates (21%, 9%, 0%) supported\n- VAT-exempt items (0% rate) don't contribute VAT\n- Example: \u20ac100 line with 10% discount and 21% VAT = \u20ac100 - \u20ac10 + \u20ac(18.90) = \u20ac108.90\n\n**Added 18 new tests covering:**\n- VAT calculations with various rates and discounts\n- VAT-exempt products\n- Mixed VAT rates and discounts on single invoice\n- Rendering with VAT display\n- Complex invoices with all features\n\nAll 106 tests passing.",
